@CC ===================================================================
@CC (SYSTEM)XMSG-START:MODE   --- GENERIC TEMPLATE ---
@CC Replace every <TOKEN> and edit the name/link/route lists for your
@CC network. See mode-files/README.md and the boot guide sections 5, 11.
@CC
@CC Start the XMSG kernel and bring up the network (names + links).
@CC Called from LOAD-MODE:BATC on every warm start.
@CC ===================================================================
@CC
@CC --- Stop then start the XMSG kernel, waiting for segments to fix ---
@SINTRAN-SERVICE-PROGRAM
@STOP-XMSG
@EXIT
@HOLD 0 0
@HOLD 2 2
@SINTRAN-SERVICE-PROGRAM
@START-XMSG
@EXIT
@HOLD 0 0
@HOLD 3 2
@CC
@CC --- Configure names, links and routing -----------------------------
@CC   <alias>   = symbolic name for a neighbour  (e.g. D100)
@CC   <node-nr> = its node number in DECIMAL      (e.g. 100)
@CC   <HDLC-UNIT> = HDLC logical unit in OCTAL     (e.g. 1360, 1362)
@CC   <via>     = a neighbour used to relay to an indirect node
@(UTILITY)XMSG-COMMAND
SET-PRIVILEGED
@CC   -- one DEFINE-REMOTE-NAME per remote node (direct AND indirect) --
DEFINE-REMOTE-NAME,,<alias-1> <node-nr-1>
DEFINE-REMOTE-NAME,,<alias-2> <node-nr-2>
@CC   -- one START-LINK per DIRECT HDLC neighbour ----------------------
START-LINK,<HDLC-UNIT-1>,,,-1,,
START-LINK,<HDLC-UNIT-2>,,,-1,,
@CC   -- for Ethernet (DLAN) neighbours use this instead of START-LINK: -
@CC DEFINE-NETWORK-CONNECTION <alias>,ENNS0,,0,0,0,0
@CC   -- for nodes reached THROUGH a neighbour, add a route: -----------
@CC DEFINE-SYSTEM-ROUTE,,<dest-alias> <via>
@CC   -- if THIS node relays traffic for others: -----------------------
ENABLE-ROUTE-THROUGH
LIST-LINKS,,,
LIST-ROUTING-INFO,,,
EXIT
@CC
@CC --- Large networks: replace the inline lists above with include ----
@CC     files pulled in from INSIDE XMSG-COMMAND, e.g.:
@CC         MODE (UTILITY)DEFINE-REMOTE:INCL,1
@CC         MODE (UTILITY)DEFINE-ETH-DLAN:INCL,1
@CC         MODE (UTILITY)DEF-ROUT-<node>:INCL,1
@CC ===================================================================
@CC END OF XMSG-START:MODE
@CC ===================================================================
